@US46 @shared
Feature: Unified alert center
  As a platform user
  I want to view, resolve and clear in one place the alerts from maintenance, IoT sensors and anomalies
  So that I act quickly on critical events

  Background:
    Given the user is signed in as an administrator

  Scenario Outline: Viewing the alerts of each source
    Given an alert generated by "<event>" is pending in the alert center
    When the administrator opens the alert center
    Then the alert is listed with source "<source>" and severity "<severity>"

    Examples:
      | event                       | source      | severity |
      | maintenance threshold       | MAINTENANCE | WARNING  |
      | motion sensor disconnection | SENSOR      | WARNING  |
      | anomaly report              | ANOMALY     | CRITICAL |

  Scenario: Pending alerts are shown by default
    Given the administrator has pending and resolved alerts
    When the administrator opens the alert center without choosing a status
    Then only the pending alerts are listed

  Scenario: Viewing resolved alerts
    Given the administrator has pending and resolved alerts
    When the administrator filters the alert center by status "RESOLVED"
    Then only the resolved alerts are listed
    And each resolved alert shows when it was resolved

  Scenario: Filtering alerts by severity
    Given the administrator has pending alerts of severity "WARNING" and "CRITICAL"
    When the administrator filters the alert center by severity "CRITICAL"
    Then only the "CRITICAL" alerts are listed

  Scenario: Resolving an alert
    Given the user has an active alert in the alert center
    When the user marks the alert as resolved
    Then the alert status changes to "Resolved"
    And the alert is no longer counted as pending

  Scenario: Clearing all resolved alerts
    Given the user has multiple resolved alerts
    When the user clears all alerts
    Then the resolved alerts for the user's role are removed from the alert center

  Scenario: Clearing a single resolved alert
    Given the administrator has a resolved alert in the alert center
    When the administrator clears that alert
    Then the alert is removed from the alert center in every status view

  Scenario: A pending alert cannot be cleared
    Given the administrator has a pending alert in the alert center
    When the administrator tries to clear that alert
    Then the request is rejected with a business rule violation (HTTP 422)
    And the alert stays pending in the alert center

  Scenario: Alerts of another administrator are not accessible
    Given an alert belongs to another administrator
    When the administrator opens the alert center
    Then the alert is not listed
    And resolving or clearing that alert is denied (HTTP 403)
